⌨️ AckuPad Setup Guide

Welcome to the Setup Guide for your AckuPad! This document will guide you through flashing the firmware onto the microcontroller and running the configuration UI on your PC.
📁 Project Structure

    RP2040 Code.ino: The firmware for the microcontroller (Arduino-based).

    AckuPad UI.ahk: The Windows configuration tool (AutoHotkey).

🛠 Step 1: Programming the Controller (Firmware)

The RP2040 (e.g., Raspberry Pi Pico or Waveshare RP2040-Zero) acts as the heart of your macropad.

    Install Arduino IDE: Download and install the Arduino IDE.

    Add Board Support:

        Go to File > Preferences.

        Add this URL to the "Additional Boards Manager URLs" field:
        https://github.com/earlephilhower/arduino-pico/releases/download/global/package_rp2040_index.json

        Go to Tools > Board > Boards Manager, search for RP2040, and install the package by Earle F. Philhower.

    Install Libraries:

        Open Sketch > Include Library > Manage Libraries.

        Search for HID-Project (by NicoHood) and install it. This allows the pad to act as a keyboard.

    Flash the Code:

        Open RP2040 Code.ino in the Arduino IDE.

        Connect your macropad to your PC via USB.

        Under Tools > Board, select your specific RP2040 board.

        Click the Upload button (arrow icon).

🖥 Step 2: Setting up the User Interface (Windows)

The UI tool allows you to assign macros graphically without having to change the Arduino code every time.

    Install AutoHotkey:

        Download and install AutoHotkey v1.1 (important: the script is written for v1.1) from autohotkey.com.

    Prepare Files:

        Ensure the image files layout_m1.png and layout_m2.png are in the same folder as AckuPad UI.ahk.

    Run the Script:

        Double-click AckuPad UI.ahk.

        A green "H" icon will appear in your system tray (bottom right corner near the clock).

    Configure:

        Click on the button areas in the app graphic to assign actions like Copy, Paste, or Media controls.

        Click SAVE to store the settings in the AckuPadSettings.ini file.

💡 Troubleshooting

    Buttons not reacting: Check the digitalRead pin mapping in the Arduino code to ensure it matches your physical wiring.

    UI not showing images: The images must be named exactly layout_m1.png and layout_m2.png and placed in the same directory as the script.

    F-Key conflict: The macropad sends F13–F24 by default. Ensure no other software is blocking these keys.

Enjoy your AckuPad! 🚀
